1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,811
Mia: Is Mommy coming home tomorrow?

2
00:00:03,111 --> 00:00:05,679
Echo: Yes, Mia. Tomorrow.

3
00:00:13,029 --> 00:00:28,382
Deep underground, in a small dark bedroom, red emergency lights flicker. Eight-year-old Mia sleeps beneath an old blanket. On the nightstand beside her rests a framed photograph... of Mia and her mother.

4
00:00:28,732 --> 00:00:36,409
ECHO-07 stands beside her bed, watching her quietly. Inside him, red warnings flash.

5
00:00:36,759 --> 00:00:39,333
Mia slowly opens her eyes.

6
00:00:39,433 --> 00:00:40,474
Mia: Echo?

7
00:00:40,394 --> 00:00:41,623
Echo: Yes, Mia?

8
00:00:41,543 --> 00:00:43,854
Mia: Is Mommy coming home tomorrow?

9
00:00:44,204 --> 00:00:51,404
A new warning flashes inside him. Echo looks toward the photograph on the nightstand... and pauses.

10
00:00:51,804 --> 00:00:54,372
Echo: Yes, Mia. Tomorrow.

11
00:00:54,722 --> 00:00:57,780
Mia smiles, and closes her eyes.

12
00:00:57,880 --> 00:00:59,359
Mia: Goodnight, Echo.

13
00:00:59,279 --> 00:01:00,429
Echo: Goodnight, Mia.

14
00:01:00,779 --> 00:01:04,636
And Echo's cyan eyes dim... with sadness.

15
00:01:06,186 --> 00:01:22,154
Morning in the underground shelter. Echo stands at a small kitchen counter as smoke rises from the toaster. At the table, Mia watches... suspiciously. Echo proudly places a plate of burnt black toast in front of her.

16
00:01:22,504 --> 00:01:24,721
Mia: You burned it again.

17
00:01:24,641 --> 00:01:28,360
Echo: Incorrect. It is eighty-seven percent toasted.

18
00:01:28,280 --> 00:01:30,501
Mia: It's BLACK!

19
00:01:30,421 --> 00:01:32,924
Echo: A desirable shade of toast.

20
00:01:33,024 --> 00:01:38,724
Mia bursts into laughter, while Echo examines the toast, looking confused.

21
00:01:38,824 --> 00:01:41,080
Echo: Would you prefer eighty-six percent?

22
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:43,565
Mia: I'd prefer bread.

23
00:01:43,915 --> 00:01:52,314
Echo tilts his head. Later, they play chess. When Echo looks away... Mia secretly moves one of his pieces.

24
00:01:52,414 --> 00:01:53,839
Echo: You are cheating.

25
00:01:53,759 --> 00:01:55,032
Mia: Prove it.

26
00:01:55,382 --> 00:02:03,952
Echo looks directly at the moved piece, his eyes narrowing... then he deliberately moves another piece, letting Mia win.

27
00:02:04,052 --> 00:02:05,291
Mia: Checkmate!

28
00:02:05,211 --> 00:02:07,185
Echo: An unexpected defeat.

29
00:02:07,535 --> 00:02:19,079
Mia celebrates, and Echo's eyes curve into a smile. Afterward, Mia draws a crayon picture of herself, Echo, and her mother, holding hands beneath a bright sun.

30
00:02:19,179 --> 00:02:22,267
Mia: When Mommy comes back, we'll all go outside together.

31
00:02:22,187 --> 00:02:24,366
Echo: That sounds... wonderful.

32
00:02:24,716 --> 00:02:27,501
Mia tapes the drawing to Echo's chest.

33
00:02:27,601 --> 00:02:29,417
Mia: Now we're a family.

34
00:02:29,767 --> 00:02:37,301
Echo looks down at the drawing. His battery drops to ten percent... and he quietly covers the warning with his hand.

35
00:02:38,851 --> 00:02:50,170
While Echo repairs equipment elsewhere, Mia explores a dim corridor with her flashlight. The beam reveals a large, locked metal door. Surface Access.

36
00:02:50,270 --> 00:02:51,823
Mia: What's behind here?

37
00:02:52,173 --> 00:02:59,845
She touches the access panel. A red lock appears... and an alarm sounds. Echo rushes into the corridor.

38
00:02:59,945 --> 00:03:02,250
Echo: Mia! Step away from the door.

39
00:03:02,170 --> 00:03:04,068
Mia: Why can't we go outside?

40
00:03:03,988 --> 00:03:05,836
Echo: The surface is unsafe.

41
00:03:06,186 --> 00:03:09,153
Mia looks at the door, then back at Echo.

42
00:03:09,253 --> 00:03:13,690
Mia: But Mommy went outside. How many days has she been gone?

43
00:03:14,040 --> 00:03:16,492
Echo becomes completely still.

44
00:03:16,592 --> 00:03:18,347
Echo: You should return to your room.

45
00:03:18,517 --> 00:03:20,325
Mia: Echo. How many?

46
00:03:20,975 --> 00:03:22,324
Echo: I do not remember.

47
00:03:22,494 --> 00:03:24,695
Mia: But you remember everything.

48
00:03:25,045 --> 00:03:30,414
Disappointed, Mia walks away... leaving Echo alone beside the door.

49
00:03:31,964 --> 00:03:36,567
That night, Mia wakes up... and Echo is gone.

50
00:03:36,667 --> 00:03:37,635
Mia: Echo?

51
00:03:37,985 --> 00:03:48,435
She follows a faint mechanical sound into a dark maintenance room. Echo is kneeling beside a damaged charging station. Sparks fly from the cables.

52
00:03:48,535 --> 00:03:52,317
Echo: Attempt twenty-seven... unsuccessful.

53
00:03:52,667 --> 00:04:04,883
Nearby, Mia notices an old computer terminal. On its screen... her mother's photograph. She presses play. Doctor Elena appears, in a flickering blue recording.

54
00:04:05,233 --> 00:04:17,759
Dr. Elena: Echo. If you're watching this, the evacuation has failed. Keep Mia safe. She's only three. She won't understand what's happening. If I don't return... promise me you won't let her lose hope.

55
00:04:18,159 --> 00:04:19,249
Echo: I promise.

56
00:04:19,599 --> 00:04:26,384
The recording ends. Startled, Mia knocks a metal container to the floor. Echo turns around.

57
00:04:26,484 --> 00:04:31,782
Mia: I was three? You've been telling me tomorrow for FIVE years?

58
00:04:31,702 --> 00:04:34,018
Echo: Mia, I was trying to...

59
00:04:34,418 --> 00:04:36,730
Mia: You lied to me!

60
00:04:37,080 --> 00:04:43,840
Mia runs out of the room. Echo stays beside the broken charger... as his eyes dim.

61
00:04:45,390 --> 00:04:53,607
Mia sits alone on her bed, hugging her red scarf. Echo approaches the closed door, carrying a small dinner tray.

62
00:04:53,957 --> 00:04:58,675
Echo: Mia. Your dinner is ready. I did not burn the toast.

63
00:04:58,845 --> 00:05:01,204
Mia: Go away.

64
00:05:01,554 --> 00:05:06,139
Echo slowly lowers the tray, and sits down against the closed door.

65
00:05:06,489 --> 00:05:08,775
Mia: You said robots can't lie.

66
00:05:08,945 --> 00:05:10,435
Echo: We are not supposed to.

67
00:05:10,605 --> 00:05:12,208
Mia: Then why did you?

68
00:05:12,558 --> 00:05:14,345
Echo looks at the floor.

69
00:05:14,445 --> 00:05:21,083
Echo: The first time I told you she would return... you stopped crying. I wanted you to smile again.

70
00:05:21,433 --> 00:05:25,291
Inside the bedroom, Mia looks at her mother's photograph.

71
00:05:25,391 --> 00:05:27,321
Mia: That doesn't make it okay.

72
00:05:27,491 --> 00:05:29,464
Echo: No. It does not.

73
00:05:30,114 --> 00:05:32,569
Mia: I hate you.

74
00:05:33,219 --> 00:05:34,192
Echo: Understood.

75
00:05:34,542 --> 00:05:43,016
He leaves the tray outside her door. Suddenly... the lights flicker. Echo looks toward the forbidden surface door.

76
00:05:44,566 --> 00:05:53,444
The whole shelter loses power. Darkness... then the red emergency lights kick on. Mia wakes up, frightened.

77
00:05:53,544 --> 00:05:54,562
Mia: Echo?

78
00:05:54,912 --> 00:05:58,325
Echo enters, holding her bright yellow raincoat.

79
00:05:58,425 --> 00:05:59,730
Echo: We have to leave.

80
00:05:59,650 --> 00:06:01,822
Mia: Leave? Where?

81
00:06:01,742 --> 00:06:02,777
Echo: Outside.

82
00:06:03,127 --> 00:06:14,859
At the Surface Access door, Echo enters an emergency override code. The heavy door slowly grinds open... and warm golden sunlight floods the dark corridor.

83
00:06:15,209 --> 00:06:28,257
Mia and Echo step out into a breathtaking, abandoned city... overgrown with green vines, blooming flowers and clear flowing streams. Birds soar across the bright sky.

84
00:06:28,607 --> 00:06:31,794
Mia: Wow... You said it wasn't safe.

85
00:06:31,714 --> 00:06:34,648
Echo: The last surface readings were five years old.

86
00:06:34,568 --> 00:06:36,149
Mia: You could've checked.

87
00:06:36,069 --> 00:06:36,905
Echo: Yes.

88
00:06:37,255 --> 00:06:42,379
A colorful butterfly flutters down, and lands on Mia's outstretched hand.

89
00:06:42,479 --> 00:06:44,646
Mia: I've never seen a real one.

90
00:06:44,996 --> 00:06:48,433
Suddenly, Echo's sensors pick up a faint signal.

91
00:06:48,533 --> 00:06:51,329
Echo: Mia. There are other people.

92
00:06:51,249 --> 00:06:52,220
Mia: Mommy?

93
00:06:52,140 --> 00:06:53,182
Echo: I don't know.

94
00:06:53,532 --> 00:06:57,121
Mia looks toward the distant radio tower on the horizon.

95
00:06:57,221 --> 00:06:58,788
Mia: Then let's find out.

96
00:07:00,338 --> 00:07:08,646
As they walk through the overgrown streets, Mia picks a small wildflower, and tucks it beside the crayon drawing on Echo's chest.

97
00:07:08,746 --> 00:07:10,581
Mia: Now you look official.

98
00:07:10,501 --> 00:07:12,344
Echo: I was already official.

99
00:07:12,694 --> 00:07:22,062
Mia smiles. By sunset, they reach an old ruined bridge leading toward the radio tower, its red beacon flashing in the distance.

100
00:07:22,412 --> 00:07:30,545
Echo's steps grow slower. His damaged arm twitches... until his knees give way, and he collapses onto the bridge.

101
00:07:30,645 --> 00:07:31,673
Mia: Echo!

102
00:07:32,023 --> 00:07:35,286
She kneels beside him as he struggles to get up.

103
00:07:35,386 --> 00:07:38,210
Echo: A temporary malfunction.

104
00:07:38,310 --> 00:07:41,198
Mia sees the flashing light on his chest.

105
00:07:41,298 --> 00:07:43,658
Mia: Stop lying!

106
00:07:43,578 --> 00:07:45,327
Echo: My battery is depleted.

107
00:07:45,247 --> 00:07:47,116
Mia: Then we'll find another one.

108
00:07:47,036 --> 00:07:51,085
Echo: There is insufficient time. You must continue without me.

109
00:07:51,435 --> 00:07:53,977
Mia shakes her head, firmly.

110
00:07:54,077 --> 00:07:55,001
Mia: No.

111
00:07:54,921 --> 00:07:55,722
Echo: Mia...

112
00:07:56,122 --> 00:07:57,825
Mia: You're my family too.

113
00:07:57,925 --> 00:08:02,997
Mia holds out her hand. A soft smile appears in Echo's eyes.

114
00:08:03,097 --> 00:08:05,455
Echo: Then we will go together.

115
00:08:05,805 --> 00:08:13,159
With her red scarf blowing in the sunset wind, Mia supports Echo's weight... as they cross the bridge together.

116
00:08:14,709 --> 00:08:24,624
Night falls as they reach the abandoned radio station. Echo examines the emergency transmitter, pressing switches... but nothing turns on.

117
00:08:24,724 --> 00:08:26,973
Echo: The transmitter has no power.

118
00:08:27,323 --> 00:08:34,497
Echo looks at the loose power cables... then down at his own chest. He picks up a heavy cable.

119
00:08:34,597 --> 00:08:36,476
Mia: What are you doing?

120
00:08:36,576 --> 00:08:40,005
Echo plugs the cable directly into his chest.

121
00:08:40,105 --> 00:08:43,039
Echo: Mia. I need you to press that button.

122
00:08:43,139 --> 00:08:44,471
She hesitates.

123
00:08:44,571 --> 00:08:45,542
Echo: Please.

124
00:08:45,892 --> 00:08:54,595
Mia presses the button. Blue lights glow across the console. Static crackles from the speaker... and then, a voice.

125
00:08:54,695 --> 00:08:57,607
Radio: Hello? Is somebody there?

126
00:08:57,957 --> 00:08:59,943
Mia grabs the microphone.

127
00:09:00,043 --> 00:09:02,997
Mia: Please help! My friend is dying!

128
00:09:02,917 --> 00:09:05,096
Radio: Stay where you are. We're coming.

129
00:09:05,446 --> 00:09:07,213
Mia turns to Echo.

130
00:09:07,313 --> 00:09:10,925
Mia: They're coming! You heard them! They'll fix you.

131
00:09:11,025 --> 00:09:15,070
Echo's eyes begin to flicker. Mia takes his hand.

132
00:09:15,170 --> 00:09:17,028
Mia: Promise me you'll be okay.

133
00:09:17,378 --> 00:09:21,187
Echo looks down at the crayon family drawing on his chest.

134
00:09:21,587 --> 00:09:22,779
Echo: I promise.

135
00:09:23,129 --> 00:09:29,076
Echo's cyan eyes slowly dim to black. His hand goes still.

136
00:09:29,476 --> 00:09:32,148
Mia: Echo? Echo!

137
00:09:32,498 --> 00:09:39,801
Mia wraps her arms around him... as the headlights of a distant rescue vehicle shine through the station windows.

138
00:09:41,351 --> 00:09:48,907
Three weeks later, morning sunlight fills a peaceful settlement, surrounded by gardens and rebuilt homes.

139
00:09:49,257 --> 00:09:56,846
Inside a warm wooden workshop, Mia waits anxiously beside Echo, as a technician connects a new power cell.

140
00:09:56,946 --> 00:09:58,604
Technician: Let's see if this works.

141
00:09:58,954 --> 00:10:03,604
Echo's systems hum to life. His cyan eyes light up.

142
00:10:03,704 --> 00:10:04,765
Mia: Echo!

143
00:10:04,685 --> 00:10:08,753
Echo: Hello. I am ECHO-07. How may I assist you?

144
00:10:09,103 --> 00:10:16,867
Mia's smile fades. Slowly, she takes out their worn crayon drawing, and places it into Echo's hands.

145
00:10:16,967 --> 00:10:19,551
Mia: It's okay. We can start again.

146
00:10:19,901 --> 00:10:26,542
She turns toward the door. Behind her, Echo looks down at the drawing... his eyes flickering.

147
00:10:26,642 --> 00:10:27,368
Echo: Mia?

148
00:10:27,468 --> 00:10:30,940
She freezes... and slowly turns around.

149
00:10:31,340 --> 00:10:33,378
Mia: You remember me?

150
00:10:34,028 --> 00:10:37,802
Echo: I remember... that you prefer your toast unburned.

151
00:10:38,152 --> 00:10:50,617
Laughing through her tears, Mia runs to him and throws her arms around him. Echo gently holds her close, their family drawing in his hand... as warm morning sunlight fills the workshop.
